  "slug": "metabolism-proteomics-41aa",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and publications pair LLM agents and no-code interfaces with multi-step workflows that run analyses end to end.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is consolidation of multi-step analysis into single executable units, accessed through natural language, no-code interfaces or automated configuration. ChatDRex runs network-based drug repurposing over the NeDRex knowledge graph through a conversational multi-agent system, and MARRVEL-MCP gives LLMs 39 tools over genomic databases for autonomous rare disease variant interpretation. Ovo bundles protein design models, Nextflow workflows, data management and visualization in one open-source platform. The Omics BioAnalytics RShiny application and the automated statistical and machine learning platform package preprocessing, modeling and dashboards for biomarker and biological data analysis. What is new is heterogeneous steps combined within one executable unit, layered with prompt-driven access; the metaviral prompt-to-pipeline evaluation and ChatDRex emphasize access more than packaging.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-30"
}
